IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap2-3val`

-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), section 2015(a) to (c) (snap2).
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text; nothing here is verified against the official text.
-- READING A RESULT. JUST TRUE: the text says yes. JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words. NOTHING: the text does not say.
-- Every branch that answers no carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`, every branch that answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- A function whose name says "is ineligible" or "shall not" answers JUST TRUE when the bar applies and JUST FALSE when the text says it does not.

§ `Section 2015(a): additional specific conditions`

-- src:493 | (a) Additional specific conditions rendering individuals ineligible
-- src:494 | In addition to meeting the standards of eligibility prescribed in section 2014 of this title, households and individuals who are members of eligible households must also meet and comply with the specific requirements of this section to be eligible for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(a) (src:493-494)
GIVEN `s 2014 the standards of eligibility are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the household or individual meets and complies with the specific requirements of this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(a) the household or individual is eligible to participate` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must also meet and comply with the specific requirements of this section to be eligible"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 2014's standards, or this section's requirements, not supplied
    `s 2015 helper: both answers hold` `s 2014 the standards of eligibility are met` `the household or individual meets and complies with the specific requirements of this section`

§ `Section 2015(b): fraud and misrepresentation`

DECLARE `s 2015(b)(1) outcome` IS ONE OF
    `s 2015(b)(1) ineligible for a period` HAS `the period` IS A `Period of ineligibility`
    `s 2015(b)(1) not covered`

-- src:496 | (1) Any person who has been found by any State or Federal court or administrative agency to have intentionally (A) made a false or misleading statement, or misrepresented, concealed or withheld facts, or (B) committed any act that constitutes a violation of this chapter, the regulations issued thereunder, or any State statute, for the purpose of using, presenting, transferring, acquiring, receiving, or possessing program benefits shall, immediately upon the rendering of such determination, become ineligible for further participation in the program—
-- src:497 | (i) for a period of 1 year upon the first occasion of any such determination;
-- src:498 | (ii) for a period of 2 years upon—
-- src:499 | (I) the second occasion of any such determination; or
-- src:500 | (II) the first occasion of a finding by a Federal, State, or local court of the trading of a controlled substance (as defined in section 802 of title 21) for benefits; and
-- src:501 | (iii) permanently upon—
-- src:502 | (I) the third occasion of any such determination;
-- src:503 | (II) the second occasion of a finding by a Federal, State, or local court of the trading of a controlled substance (as defined in section 802 of title 21) for benefits;
-- src:504 | (III) the first occasion of a finding by a Federal, State, or local court of the trading of firearms, ammunition, or explosives for benefits; or
-- src:505 | (IV) a conviction of an offense under subsection (b) or (c) of section 2024 of this title involving an item covered by subsection (b) or (c) of section 2024 of this title having a value of $500 or more.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(b)(1) (src:496-505)
GIVEN `found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `intentionally made a false or misleading statement, or misrepresented, concealed or withheld facts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `intentionally committed an act that violates this chapter, its regulations or a State statute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for the purpose of using, presenting, transferring, acquiring, receiving or possessing program benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occasion of such a determination, counting from 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the occasion of a court finding of trading a controlled substance for benefits, 0 if none` IS A NUMBER
      `a court has found, for the first occasion, the trading of firearms, ammunition or explosives for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `convicted of an offense under subsection (b) or (c) of section 2024 involving a covered item` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of that item in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 2015(b)(1) outcome`
`s 2015(b)(1) the period of ineligibility the finding carries` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who has been found by any State or Federal court or administrative agency to have intentionally ... for the purpose of"; the paragraph speaks only of that class and does not say that anyone else is not ineligible (reading (b), see NOTES)
        IF NOT (`found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency`
                AND (`intentionally made a false or misleading statement, or misrepresented, concealed or withheld facts`
                     OR `intentionally committed an act that violates this chapter, its regulations or a State statute`)
                AND `for the purpose of using, presenting, transferring, acquiring, receiving or possessing program benefits`)
            THEN `s 2015(b)(1) not covered`
        -- clause (iii): permanently upon (I) the third occasion, (II) the second court finding on a controlled substance, (III) the first court finding on firearms, (IV) a conviction of $500 or more
        IF `the occasion of such a determination, counting from 1` AT LEAST 3
           OR `the occasion of a court finding of trading a controlled substance for benefits, 0 if none` AT LEAST 2
           OR `a court has found, for the first occasion, the trading of firearms, ammunition or explosives for benefits`
           OR (`convicted of an offense under subsection (b) or (c) of section 2024 involving a covered item` AND `the value of that item in dollars` AT LEAST 500)
            THEN `s 2015(b)(1) ineligible for a period` `permanently`
        -- clause (ii): 2 years upon (I) the second occasion or (II) the first court finding on a controlled substance
        IF `the occasion of such a determination, counting from 1` EQUALS 2
           OR `the occasion of a court finding of trading a controlled substance for benefits, 0 if none` EQUALS 1
            THEN `s 2015(b)(1) ineligible for a period` (`for a number of years` 2)
        -- clause (i): 1 year upon the first occasion
        IF `the occasion of such a determination, counting from 1` EQUALS 1
            THEN `s 2015(b)(1) ineligible for a period` (`for a number of years` 1)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a determination counted below the first occasion is not described by the paragraph
        OTHERWISE `s 2015(b)(1) not covered`

-- src:506 | During the period of such ineligibility, no household shall receive increased benefits under this chapter as the result of a member of such household having been disqualified under this subsection.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(b)(1), closing words (src:506-506)
GIVEN `the member was disqualified under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of ineligibility is running` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household's increase in benefits is the result of that disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(b)(1) the household may receive increased benefits as the result of the member's disqualification` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no household shall receive increased benefits under this chapter as the result of a member of such household having been disqualified"
        IF `the member was disqualified under subsection (b)` AND `the period of ineligibility is running` AND `the household's increase in benefits is the result of that disqualification`
            THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for "the period of such ineligibility" and for an increase "as the result of" the disqualification only
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2015(b)(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 2015(b)(2) proceed by an administrative hearing`
    `s 2015(b)(2) refer the matter for civil or criminal action in a court of law`

-- src:507 | (2) Each State agency shall proceed against an individual alleged to have engaged in such activity either by way of administrative hearings, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing at the State level, or by referring such matters to appropriate authorities for civil or criminal action in a court of law.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(b)(2) (src:507-507)
GIVEN `the individual is alleged to have engaged in such activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency proceeds by an administrative hearing, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing at the State level` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency refers the matter to appropriate authorities for civil or criminal action in a court of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(b)(2) the State agency has proceeded against the individual in a way the paragraph provides` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the individual is alleged to have engaged in such activity` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "an individual alleged to have engaged in such activity"
        IF `the State agency proceeds by an administrative hearing, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing at the State level`
           OR `the State agency refers the matter to appropriate authorities for civil or criminal action in a court of law` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall proceed against an individual alleged to have engaged in such activity either by way of administrative hearings ... or by referring such matters to appropriate authorities" (reading (a), stretched: the text has no "if" here and none of the brief's other FALSE words; the no rests on "either ... or" naming the two ways the paragraph provides, so a way that is neither is not one it provides; the paragraph is silent on whether a third way is barred, and this function does not ask that)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:507 | (2) Each State agency shall proceed against an individual alleged to have engaged in such activity either by way of administrative hearings, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing at the State level, or by referring such matters to appropriate authorities for civil or criminal action in a court of law.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(b)(2) (src:507-507)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 2015(b)(2) action`
`s 2015(b)(2) the State agency must proceed against the individual` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `s 2015(b)(2) proceed by an administrative hearing`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:508 | (3) Such periods of ineligibility as are provided for in paragraph (1) of this subsection shall remain in effect, without possibility of administrative stay, unless and until the finding upon which the ineligibility is based is subsequently reversed by a court of appropriate jurisdiction, but in no event shall the period of ineligibility be subject to review.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(b)(3) (src:508-508)
GIVEN `the period of ineligibility is one provided for in paragraph (1) of subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the finding on which the ineligibility is based has been reversed by a court of appropriate jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(b)(3) the period of ineligibility remains in effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the period of ineligibility is one provided for in paragraph (1) of subsection (b)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Such periods of ineligibility as are provided for in paragraph (1)"
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless and until the finding upon which the ineligibility is based is subsequently reversed by a court of appropriate jurisdiction"
        IF `the finding on which the ineligibility is based has been reversed by a court of appropriate jurisdiction` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:508 | (3) Such periods of ineligibility as are provided for in paragraph (1) of this subsection shall remain in effect, without possibility of administrative stay, unless and until the finding upon which the ineligibility is based is subsequently reversed by a court of appropriate jurisdiction, but in no event shall the period of ineligibility be subject to review.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(b)(3) (src:508-508)
GIVEN `the period of ineligibility is one provided for in paragraph (1) of subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(b)(3) the period of ineligibility can be stayed administratively or reviewed` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without possibility of administrative stay"
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in no event shall the period of ineligibility be subject to review"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): any other period of ineligibility
    IF `the period of ineligibility is one provided for in paragraph (1) of subsection (b)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:509 | (4) The Secretary shall prescribe such regulations as the Secretary may deem appropriate to ensure that information concerning any such determination with respect to a specific individual is forwarded to the Office of the Secretary by any appropriate State or Federal entity for the use of the Secretary in administering the provisions of this section. No State shall withhold such information from the Secretary or the Secretary’s designee for any reason whatsoever.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(b)(4) (src:509-509)
GIVEN `the information concerns a determination with respect to a specific individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(b)(4) the State may withhold the information from the Secretary` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No State shall withhold such information from the Secretary or the Secretary’s designee for any reason whatsoever"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): information that is not "any such determination with respect to a specific individual"
    IF `the information concerns a determination with respect to a specific individual` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 2015(c): refusal to provide information, and periodic reporting`

-- src:510 | (c) Refusal to provide necessary information
-- src:511 | Except in a case in which a household is receiving transitional benefits during the transitional benefits period under section 2020(s) of this title, no household shall be eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if it refuses to cooperate in providing information to the State agency that is necessary for making a determination of its eligibility or for completing any subsequent review of its eligibility.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c) (src:510-511)
GIVEN `s 2020(s) the household is receiving transitional benefits during the transitional benefits period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household refuses to cooperate in providing information to the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is necessary for a determination of eligibility or for completing a subsequent review of eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c) the household is ineligible for refusing to provide necessary information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except in a case in which a household is receiving transitional benefits during the transitional benefits period"
        IF `s 2020(s) the household is receiving transitional benefits during the transitional benefits period` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it refuses to cooperate in providing information" (reading (a): a failed "if")
        IF NOT `the household refuses to cooperate in providing information to the State agency` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "necessary for making a determination of its eligibility or for completing any subsequent review of its eligibility" (reading (a))
        IF NOT `the information is necessary for a determination of eligibility or for completing a subsequent review of eligibility` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:513 | (A) A State agency may require certain categories of households to file periodic reports of income and household circumstances in accordance with standards prescribed by the Secretary, except that a State agency may not require periodic reporting—
-- src:514 | (i) for periods shorter than 4 months by migrant or seasonal farmworker households;
-- src:515 | (ii) for periods shorter than 4 months by households in which all members are homeless individuals; or
-- src:516 | (iii) for periods shorter than 1 year by households that have no earned income and in which all adult members are elderly or disabled.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(1)(A) (src:513-516)
GIVEN `the length of the reporting period in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the household is a migrant or seasonal farmworker household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(l) all members of the household are homeless individuals` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the household has earned income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(j) all adult members of the household are elderly or disabled members` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirement accords with the standards prescribed by the Secretary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(1)(A) the State agency may require periodic reports for the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a State agency may not require periodic reporting"
        IF `the barred` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a bar applies depends on an answer of section 2012 not supplied
        IF `the barred` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- the grant is "in accordance with standards prescribed by the Secretary", which the text does not state
        IF `the requirement accords with the standards prescribed by the Secretary` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the barred` MEANS
            `s 2015 helper: at least one answer holds` `clause (i) bars it` (`s 2015 helper: at least one answer holds` `clause (ii) bars it` `clause (iii) bars it`)
        `clause (i) bars it` MEANS
            JUST (`the household is a migrant or seasonal farmworker household` AND `the length of the reporting period in months` LESS THAN 4)
        `clause (ii) bars it` MEANS
            `s 2015 helper: both answers hold` (JUST (`the length of the reporting period in months` LESS THAN 4)) `s 2012(l) all members of the household are homeless individuals`
        `clause (iii) bars it` MEANS
            `s 2015 helper: both answers hold` (JUST ((NOT `the household has earned income`) AND `the length of the reporting period in months` LESS THAN 12)) `s 2012(j) all adult members of the household are elderly or disabled members`

-- src:517 | (B) Each household that is not required to file such periodic reports shall be required to report or cause to be reported to the State agency changes in income or household circumstances that the Secretary considers necessary to assure accurate eligibility and benefit determinations.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(1)(B) (src:517-517)
GIVEN `the household is not required to file periodic reports` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary considers the change necessary to assure accurate eligibility and benefit determinations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(1)(B) the household is required to report the change in income or household circumstances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence reaches "Each household that is not required to file such periodic reports"
        IF NOT `the household is not required to file periodic reports` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the Secretary considers the change necessary to assure accurate eligibility and benefit determinations` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what "the Secretary considers necessary" is not stated
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:518 | (C) A State agency may require periodic reporting on a monthly basis by households residing on a reservation only if—
-- src:519 | (i) the State agency reinstates benefits, without requiring a new application, for any household residing on a reservation that submits a report not later than 1 month after the end of the month in which benefits would otherwise be provided;
-- src:520 | (ii) the State agency does not delay, reduce, suspend, or terminate the allotment of a household that submits a report not later than 1 month after the end of the month in which the report is due;
-- src:521 | (iii) on March 25, 1994, the State agency requires households residing on a reservation to file periodic reports on a monthly basis; and
-- src:522 | (iv) the certification period for households residing on a reservation that are required to file periodic reports on a monthly basis is 2 years, unless the State demonstrates just cause to the Secretary for a shorter certification period.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(1)(C) (src:518-522)
GIVEN `s 2012(n) the household resides on a reservation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the State agency reinstates benefits, without a new application, for a reservation household that reports within 1 month after the month in which benefits would otherwise be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency does not delay, reduce, suspend or terminate the allotment of a household that reports within 1 month after the month in which the report is due` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on March 25, 1994 the State agency required households residing on a reservation to file periodic reports on a monthly basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certification period of those households in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the State demonstrates just cause to the Secretary for a shorter certification period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(1)(C) the State agency may require monthly periodic reporting by households on a reservation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subparagraph speaks of "households residing on a reservation"
        IF `s 2012(n) the household resides on a reservation` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
        IF `s 2012(n) the household resides on a reservation` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if" clause (i)
        IF NOT `the State agency reinstates benefits, without a new application, for a reservation household that reports within 1 month after the month in which benefits would otherwise be provided` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if" clause (ii)
        IF NOT `the State agency does not delay, reduce, suspend or terminate the allotment of a household that reports within 1 month after the month in which the report is due` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if" clause (iii)
        IF NOT `on March 25, 1994 the State agency required households residing on a reservation to file periodic reports on a monthly basis` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if" clause (iv): "is 2 years, unless the State demonstrates just cause"
        IF (NOT (`the certification period of those households in months` EQUALS 24)) AND (NOT `the State demonstrates just cause to the Secretary for a shorter certification period`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only if" makes the four clauses necessary and does not say they are enough
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:523 | (D) Frequency of reporting.—
-- src:524 | (i) In general.—
-- src:525 | Except as provided in subparagraphs (A) and (C), a State agency may require households that report on a periodic basis to submit reports—
-- src:526 | (I) not less often than once each 6 months; but
-- src:527 | (II) not more often than once each month.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(1)(D)(i) (src:523-527)
GIVEN `the household reports on a periodic basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subparagraph (A) or (C) provides otherwise for the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interval between reports in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(1)(D)(i) the State agency may require reports at the interval` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except as provided in subparagraphs (A) and (C)" and "households that report on a periodic basis"
        IF `subparagraph (A) or (C) provides otherwise for the household` OR (NOT `the household reports on a periodic basis`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an interval of nothing or less is not an interval between reports
        IF `the interval between reports in months` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING
        IF `the interval between reports in months` AT LEAST 1 AND `the interval between reports in months` AT MOST 6 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not less often than once each 6 months; but (II) not more often than once each month" (both bounds are worded with "not", like "not less than 30 days but not more than 90 days" in s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(VII) and "not more than 3 years" in s 2015(d)(2); s 2029(e), "of up to thirty days", has no negative in its wording and answers NOTHING outside its bound)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:528 | (ii) Reporting by households with excess income.—
-- src:529 | A household required to report less often than once each 3 months shall, notwithstanding subparagraph (B), report in a manner prescribed by the Secretary if the income of the household for any month exceeds the income standard of eligibility established under section 2014(c)(2) of this title.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(1)(D)(ii) (src:528-529)
GIVEN `the interval between reports in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the income of the household for the month in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `s 2014(c)(2) the income standard of eligibility in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(1)(D)(ii) the household must report in the manner the Secretary prescribes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A household required to report less often than once each 3 months"; the subparagraph speaks only of that class (reading (b), see NOTES)
        IF `the interval between reports in months` AT MOST 3 THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the income of the household for any month exceeds the income standard of eligibility" (reading (a))
        IF `the income of the household for the month in dollars` AT MOST `s 2014(c)(2) the income standard of eligibility in dollars` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:530 | (2) Any household required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1) of this subsection shall, (A) if it is eligible to participate and has filed a timely and complete report, receive its allotment, based on the reported information for a given month, within thirty days of the end of that month unless the Secretary determines that a longer period of time is necessary, (B) have available special procedures that permit the filing of the required information in the event all adult members of the household are mentally or physically handicapped or lacking in reading or writing skills to such a degree as to be unable to fill out the required forms, (C) have a reasonable period of time after the close of the month in which to file their reports on State agency designed forms, (D) be afforded prompt notice of failure to file any report timely or completely, and given a reasonable opportunity to cure that failure (with any applicable time requirements extended accordingly) and to exercise its rights under section 2020(e)(10) of this title, and (E) be provided each month (or other applicable period) with an appropriate, simple form for making the required reports of the household together with clear instructions explaining how to complete the form and the rights and responsibilities of the household under any periodic reporting system.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(2)(A) (src:530-530)
GIVEN `the month's last day` IS A DATE
      `the household is eligible to participate and has filed a timely and complete report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has determined that a longer period of time is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the longer period the Secretary determined, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 2015(c)(2)(A) the date by which the allotment must be received` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement is for a household that "is eligible to participate and has filed a timely and complete report"
        IF NOT `the household is eligible to participate and has filed a timely and complete report` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the Secretary has determined that a longer period of time is necessary` THEN JUST (`the month's last day` PLUS `the longer period the Secretary determined, in days`)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the month's last day` PLUS 30)

DECLARE `s 2015(c)(2)(A) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 2015(c)(2)(A) issue the allotment to the household`

-- src:530 | (2) Any household required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1) of this subsection shall, (A) if it is eligible to participate and has filed a timely and complete report, receive its allotment, based on the reported information for a given month, within thirty days of the end of that month unless the Secretary determines that a longer period of time is necessary, (B) have available special procedures that permit the filing of the required information in the event all adult members of the household are mentally or physically handicapped or lacking in reading or writing skills to such a degree as to be unable to fill out the required forms, (C) have a reasonable period of time after the close of the month in which to file their reports on State agency designed forms, (D) be afforded prompt notice of failure to file any report timely or completely, and given a reasonable opportunity to cure that failure (with any applicable time requirements extended accordingly) and to exercise its rights under section 2020(e)(10) of this title, and (E) be provided each month (or other applicable period) with an appropriate, simple form for making the required reports of the household together with clear instructions explaining how to complete the form and the rights and responsibilities of the household under any periodic reporting system.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(2)(A) (src:530-530)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 2015(c)(2)(A) action`
`s 2015(c)(2)(A) the State agency must give the household its allotment within thirty days of the end of the month` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `s 2015(c)(2)(A) issue the allotment to the household`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "the allotment was not given within thirty days of the end of the month"

-- src:530 | (2) Any household required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1) of this subsection shall, (A) if it is eligible to participate and has filed a timely and complete report, receive its allotment, based on the reported information for a given month, within thirty days of the end of that month unless the Secretary determines that a longer period of time is necessary, (B) have available special procedures that permit the filing of the required information in the event all adult members of the household are mentally or physically handicapped or lacking in reading or writing skills to such a degree as to be unable to fill out the required forms, (C) have a reasonable period of time after the close of the month in which to file their reports on State agency designed forms, (D) be afforded prompt notice of failure to file any report timely or completely, and given a reasonable opportunity to cure that failure (with any applicable time requirements extended accordingly) and to exercise its rights under section 2020(e)(10) of this title, and (E) be provided each month (or other applicable period) with an appropriate, simple form for making the required reports of the household together with clear instructions explaining how to complete the form and the rights and responsibilities of the household under any periodic reporting system.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(2)(B) (src:530-530)
GIVEN `the household is required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every adult member is mentally or physically handicapped or lacks reading or writing skills to such a degree as to be unable to fill out the required forms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(2)(B) the household is to have special procedures available for filing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "Any household required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1)"
        IF NOT `the household is required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1)` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the event all adult members of the household are" unable (reading (a): a failed condition)
        IF NOT `every adult member is mentally or physically handicapped or lacks reading or writing skills to such a degree as to be unable to fill out the required forms` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:530 | (2) Any household required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1) of this subsection shall, (A) if it is eligible to participate and has filed a timely and complete report, receive its allotment, based on the reported information for a given month, within thirty days of the end of that month unless the Secretary determines that a longer period of time is necessary, (B) have available special procedures that permit the filing of the required information in the event all adult members of the household are mentally or physically handicapped or lacking in reading or writing skills to such a degree as to be unable to fill out the required forms, (C) have a reasonable period of time after the close of the month in which to file their reports on State agency designed forms, (D) be afforded prompt notice of failure to file any report timely or completely, and given a reasonable opportunity to cure that failure (with any applicable time requirements extended accordingly) and to exercise its rights under section 2020(e)(10) of this title, and (E) be provided each month (or other applicable period) with an appropriate, simple form for making the required reports of the household together with clear instructions explaining how to complete the form and the rights and responsibilities of the household under any periodic reporting system.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(2)(C) to (E) (src:530-530)
GIVEN `the household is required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household failed to file a report timely or completely` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(2)(D) the household is to be given prompt notice of the failure and a reasonable opportunity to cure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only a household required to file, and only on "failure to file any report timely or completely"
        IF NOT `the household is required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1)` THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `the household failed to file a report timely or completely` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:530 | (2) Any household required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1) of this subsection shall, (A) if it is eligible to participate and has filed a timely and complete report, receive its allotment, based on the reported information for a given month, within thirty days of the end of that month unless the Secretary determines that a longer period of time is necessary, (B) have available special procedures that permit the filing of the required information in the event all adult members of the household are mentally or physically handicapped or lacking in reading or writing skills to such a degree as to be unable to fill out the required forms, (C) have a reasonable period of time after the close of the month in which to file their reports on State agency designed forms, (D) be afforded prompt notice of failure to file any report timely or completely, and given a reasonable opportunity to cure that failure (with any applicable time requirements extended accordingly) and to exercise its rights under section 2020(e)(10) of this title, and (E) be provided each month (or other applicable period) with an appropriate, simple form for making the required reports of the household together with clear instructions explaining how to complete the form and the rights and responsibilities of the household under any periodic reporting system.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(2)(C) and (E) (src:530-530)
GIVEN `the household is required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(2)(C) and (E) the household is to have a reasonable period to file and a simple form with clear instructions each month` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "Any household required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1)"
    IF `the household is required to file a periodic report under paragraph (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:531 | (3) Reports required to be filed under paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be considered complete if they contain the information relevant to eligibility and benefit determinations that is specified by the State agency. All report forms, including those related to periodic reports of circumstances, shall contain a description, in understandable terms in prominent and bold face lettering, of the appropriate civil and criminal provisions dealing with violations of this chapter including the prescribed penalties. Reports required to be filed monthly under paragraph (1) shall be the sole reporting requirement for subject matter included in such reports. In promulgating regulations implementing these reporting requirements, the Secretary shall consult with the Commissioner of Social Security and the Secretary of Health and Human Services, and, wherever feasible, households that receive assistance under title IV–A of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.] and that are required to file comparable reports under that Act [42 U.S.C. 301 et seq.] shall be provided the opportunity to file reports at the same time for purposes of this chapter and the Social Security Act.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(3) (src:531-531)
GIVEN `the report contains the information relevant to eligibility and benefit determinations that the State agency specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(3) the report is considered complete` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be considered complete if they contain the information" (reading (a): a failed "if")
    IF `the report contains the information relevant to eligibility and benefit determinations that the State agency specifies` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:531 | (3) Reports required to be filed under paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be considered complete if they contain the information relevant to eligibility and benefit determinations that is specified by the State agency. All report forms, including those related to periodic reports of circumstances, shall contain a description, in understandable terms in prominent and bold face lettering, of the appropriate civil and criminal provisions dealing with violations of this chapter including the prescribed penalties. Reports required to be filed monthly under paragraph (1) shall be the sole reporting requirement for subject matter included in such reports. In promulgating regulations implementing these reporting requirements, the Secretary shall consult with the Commissioner of Social Security and the Secretary of Health and Human Services, and, wherever feasible, households that receive assistance under title IV–A of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.] and that are required to file comparable reports under that Act [42 U.S.C. 301 et seq.] shall be provided the opportunity to file reports at the same time for purposes of this chapter and the Social Security Act.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(3) (src:531-531)
GIVEN `the form is a report form, including a periodic report of circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(3) the form is to carry a description of the civil and criminal provisions and penalties in prominent bold face lettering` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "All report forms, including those related to periodic reports of circumstances"
    IF `the form is a report form, including a periodic report of circumstances` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:531 | (3) Reports required to be filed under paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be considered complete if they contain the information relevant to eligibility and benefit determinations that is specified by the State agency. All report forms, including those related to periodic reports of circumstances, shall contain a description, in understandable terms in prominent and bold face lettering, of the appropriate civil and criminal provisions dealing with violations of this chapter including the prescribed penalties. Reports required to be filed monthly under paragraph (1) shall be the sole reporting requirement for subject matter included in such reports. In promulgating regulations implementing these reporting requirements, the Secretary shall consult with the Commissioner of Social Security and the Secretary of Health and Human Services, and, wherever feasible, households that receive assistance under title IV–A of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.] and that are required to file comparable reports under that Act [42 U.S.C. 301 et seq.] shall be provided the opportunity to file reports at the same time for purposes of this chapter and the Social Security Act.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(3) (src:531-531)
GIVEN `the report is required to be filed monthly under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subject matter is included in such monthly reports` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(3) a further reporting requirement may be imposed for the subject matter` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Reports required to be filed monthly under paragraph (1) shall be the sole reporting requirement for subject matter included in such reports"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): reports not filed monthly, and subject matter not included in them
    IF `the report is required to be filed monthly under paragraph (1)` AND `the subject matter is included in such monthly reports` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:531 | (3) Reports required to be filed under paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be considered complete if they contain the information relevant to eligibility and benefit determinations that is specified by the State agency. All report forms, including those related to periodic reports of circumstances, shall contain a description, in understandable terms in prominent and bold face lettering, of the appropriate civil and criminal provisions dealing with violations of this chapter including the prescribed penalties. Reports required to be filed monthly under paragraph (1) shall be the sole reporting requirement for subject matter included in such reports. In promulgating regulations implementing these reporting requirements, the Secretary shall consult with the Commissioner of Social Security and the Secretary of Health and Human Services, and, wherever feasible, households that receive assistance under title IV–A of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.] and that are required to file comparable reports under that Act [42 U.S.C. 301 et seq.] shall be provided the opportunity to file reports at the same time for purposes of this chapter and the Social Security Act.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(3) (src:531-531)
GIVEN `the household receives assistance under title IV-A of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household is required to file comparable reports under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is feasible to let the household file at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(3) the household is to be given the opportunity to file reports at the same time under both Acts` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "wherever feasible", and only for households that receive title IV-A assistance and file comparable reports
    IF `the household receives assistance under title IV-A of the Social Security Act` AND `the household is required to file comparable reports under that Act` AND `it is feasible to let the household file at the same time`
        THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:532 | (4) Except as provided in paragraph (1)(C), any household that fails to submit periodic reports required by paragraph (1) shall not receive an allotment for the payment period to which the unsubmitted report applies until such report is submitted.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(4) (src:532-532)
GIVEN `the household fails to submit a periodic report required by paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (1)(C) provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report has since been submitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(4) the household shall not receive an allotment for the payment period to which the report applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as provided in paragraph (1)(C)"
        IF `paragraph (1)(C) provides otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any household that fails to submit periodic reports required by paragraph (1)"
        IF NOT `the household fails to submit a periodic report required by paragraph (1)` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until such report is submitted"
        IF `the report has since been submitted` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:533 | (5) The Secretary is authorized, upon the request of a State agency, to waive any provisions of this subsection (except the provisions of the first sentence of paragraph (1) which relate to households which are not required to file periodic reports) to the extent necessary to permit the State agency to establish periodic reporting requirements for purposes of this chapter which are similar to the periodic reporting requirements established under the State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) in that State.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(c)(5) (src:533-533)
GIVEN `the State agency has requested the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is one of the first sentence of paragraph (1) that relate to households not required to file periodic reports` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the waiver is necessary to permit reporting requirements similar to those of the State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(c)(5) the Secretary is authorized to waive the provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(except the provisions of the first sentence of paragraph (1) which relate to households which are not required to file periodic reports)"
        IF `the provision is one of the first sentence of paragraph (1) that relate to households not required to file periodic reports` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon the request of a State agency" and "to the extent necessary"
        IF (NOT `the State agency has requested the waiver`) OR (NOT `the waiver is necessary to permit reporting requirements similar to those of the State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act`) THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
